    "title": "FUDGE Foundation headquarters in final stage of construction - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Southall ,\n2 hours ago\nDAYTON, Ohio ( WDTN ) – The combined FUDGE Foundation headquarters and new community resource center is in the final stages of construction as of Wednesday, Oct. 1.\nMembers of the Job Corps and Local 132 apprenticeship program were reported to be pouring cement as they worked to finish up the building.\n“I think that right now more than ever, we need a center for youth to learn,” said Tevaun Stephens, a Dayton resident. “So, I definitely think that this is dope and beneficial for the community.”\nThe building doubles as a community center and as the headquarters for Dion Green’s FUDGE Foundation , which aims to support individuals in their healing from traumatic events.\nThe FUDGE Foundation was established in 2020, a year after Green’s father lost his life in a mass shooting. Now, Green seeks to use his experience to help others.\nMoving forward 6 years after Oregon District shooting “He’s a community leader,” said Stephens. “I wanted to come out and show support.”\nThe foundation is still looking for volunteers to help with electrical, plumbing, and HVAC work in the new community resource center.\nFor more information about volunteering or donating, visit the FUDGE Foundation’s website .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
